  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "A carboxylic acid is stronger acid than phenol, hence both III and IV are stronger acids than both I and II. Also IV has a methyl group that gives electron donating inductive effect and decreases the acid strength. Therefore, III is stronger acid that IV. Between I and II, the dominant electron withdrawing inductive effect of chlorine increases acid strength of phenol slightly, hence II is stronger acid than I. Thus, the overall order is :\n(a) III $>$ IV $>$ II $>$ I",
    "image": null
  },
